$ is called an $\varepsilon$-approximate conference key state, for $\varepsilon\in[0,1]$, if there exists a conference key state $\gamma^c_{\vv{K} E}$ such that~\cite{AH09}
\begin{equation}
F\(\gamma^c_{\vv{K} E},\rho_{\vv{K}E}\)\geq 1-\varepsilon. 
\end{equation} 

\begin{definition}\label{def:multi-priv-state}
A state $\gamma_{\vv{SM}}$, with $|K_i|=K$ for all $i\in[M]$ is called a ($M$-partite) private state if and only if 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:multi-priv-state}
